From 7bb768d45d25187bc49ee2176a2364cee70deec6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:47:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge: the quad of the GUI packer decides together;
 black and opaque GUI texels cost less

A quad that went apart before its values were swapped showed wrong chroma on a few odd pixels
(12 of a frame, under black and opaque GUI, on zink): subgroup operations after divergent control
flow are not defined to see their neighbours. The packer that reads the GUI in place (PACK_GUI)
now keeps each quad together until the swap: what may be skipped is skipped only where the whole
quad can skip it (quad_any(), quad_all(): swaps with the horizontal and vertical neighbour, outside
any branch), the reads of the planes take the value outside the picture after a clamped fetch, and
each pixel's own case is chosen after. PACK (the picture composited first) is made as written
again: its quad form measured no faster (56.0 against 59.7 ms with a GUI over half the raster).

Two savings, the same values:
- a black GUI texel is light 0, which the sRGB EOTF, the matrix and the GUI white leave exactly +0:
  its PQ signal is gui_pq() of that 0, taken from the texel itself, once for the three components
  (two powers of the nine). CroqueMr's composite skips the transfer work of black GUI pixels too.
- an opaque one (alpha 1): the picture under it times 1 - a = 0 is nothing; it is not read, in the
  composite of the GUI and in drawn_over(), whose two forms then return the conversion of what was
  drawn over.
In the programs without quad operations both are taken pixel by pixel; with them, quad by quad.

Bytes, host: the 18 cases of the matrix (profile 7 FEL, its base layer alone, HDR10+ as Dolby
Vision; GUI in place and composited first; black panel, black alpha ramp, black and white strokes,
an opaque panel with marks) identical to before on llvmpipe and zink. Mutants: the black value
off by 1e-4 (each form), the opaque composite scaled, quad_all() taken as quad_any(), the chroma
codes swapped, all change the bytes; with the even pixel's values never taken from the quad, the
same bytes.

GPU time of the packing, before this series and after it: zink, GUI in place over half the raster
93.5 to 80.7 ms (FEL), 112.5 to 81.1 (HDR10+ as DV); a band 77.4 to 65.3, base layer alone 80.2
to 66.8; composited first 59.2 to 56.9; nothing drawn over 18.0 and 17.4. llvmpipe (no quad
operations): 87.6 to 78.5, 98.4 to 92.4, 65.6 to 58.2, 74.0 to 66.0, composited first 45.6 to 44.1.
